     "text": "Certainly. Below is a **Linear Regression class** implemented in Python, following the latest coding guidelines provided by your mentor, including the use of prefix notation for method and variable names, and the emphasis on consistency and readability.\n\n---\n\n### **LinearRegression Class**\n\n```python\nclass LinearRegression:\n    def __init__(self, prefix='o_'):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initialize the Linear Regression model with the specified prefix for method and variable names.\n        \n        Args:\n            prefix (str): The prefix to use for method and variable names. Default is 'o_'.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.prefix = prefix\n        self.coefficients = None\n        self.intercept = None\n        self.X = None\n        self.Y = None\n\n    def train(self, X, Y, learning_rate=0.01, epochs=100):\n        \"\"\"\n        Train the Linear Regression model using gradient descent.\n        \n        Args:\n            X (array-like): Input features.\n            Y (array-like): Target values.\n            learning_rate (float): Learning rate for gradient descent.\n            epochs (int): Number of iterations to perform.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.X = X\n        self.Y = Y\n\n        # Convert to numpy arrays for easier manipulation\n        X_np = np.array(X)\n        Y_np = np.array(Y)\n\n        # Add a column of ones to X for the intercept term\n        X_with_intercept = np.hstack((np.ones((X_np.shape[0], 1)), X_np))\n\n        # Initialize coefficients\n        self.coefficients = np.zeros(X_with_intercept.shape[1])\n        self.intercept = 0.0\n\n        # Gradient descent\n        for epoch in range(epochs):\n            # Predict\n            Y_pred = np.dot(X_with_intercept, self.coefficients) + self.intercept\n\n            # Compute gradients\n            gradient_coeff = (np.dot(X_with_intercept.T, Y_pred - Y_np)) / X_np.shape[0]\n            gradient_intercept = (np.dot(np.ones(X_np.shape[0]), Y_pred - Y_np)) / X_np